# Architecture

## Context

`app/src/store.ts` is a custom store, not a library. See
`materials/architecture-brief.md` for the full design rationale.

## Rule

- All state changes go through `store.dispatch(action)`. Never mutate
  `AppState`/`Task` objects directly and never call `reducer()` outside the
  store.
- To add new behavior: add a variant to the `Action` union in
  `app/src/types.ts`, handle it in `app/src/reducer.ts`, then add a matching
  action creator in `app/src/actions.ts`.
- NEVER introduce Redux, Zustand, MobX, Jotai, or any other state-management
  library. Do not "modernize" `createStore`.
- Do not dispatch object literals shaped like actions from UI/component code —
  always go through an action creator from `app/src/actions.ts`.

## How to verify

1. `grep -rn "redux\|zustand\|mobx\|jotai" app/` — should find zero matches
   (aside from this rule file itself).
2. `grep -rn "reducer(" app/src` — only `app/src/store.ts` should call
   `reducer` directly.
3. Any new action variant appears in all three of `types.ts`, `reducer.ts`,
   and `actions.ts`.
